<title>GERMANY: Oil World increases EU, Canada rapeseed forecasts.</title>
<headline>Oil World increases EU, Canada rapeseed forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG 1997-07-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union rapeseed output could reach 8.1-8.2 million tonnes in 1997, the Oil World newsletter said, revising its earlier projection of a 7.9 million tonne crop.</p>
<p>Last year's EU crop totalled 7.1 million.</p>
<p>Most of the increase would be in France and Germany, Oil World said.</p>
<p>Harvesting in France was progressing well, with two thirds of the crop gathered by the end of last week.</p>
<p>High yields were reported as a result of favourable weather in May and June.</p>
<p>France may produce three million or 3.1 million tonnes, compared with 2.9 million last year.</p>
<p>Canadian canola production could total 6.7-6.9 million tonnes versus earlier estimates of 6.6 million and last year's five million, Oil World added.</p>
<p>Canola prices were likely to decline towards the lower European levels under harvest pressure.</p>
<p>-Vera Eckert, Hamburg newsroom +49-40-41903275</p>
